With `.screen { display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; overflow-y:auto }`, a modal taller than viewport gets centered and top/bottom overflow, scrollable but initially top cut off? In screenshot top is visible (kicker at y18) and bottom cut. The flex centering with overflow can make top inaccessible in some browsers. Here top visible but scroll bar. We should handle short landscape.

Add CSS for max-height 480 landscape:
- .dim-screen { align-items: flex-start; padding: 8px ... }
- .modal { margin: auto 0? } Better: keep centered but reduce sizes.
- .modal { padding: 12px 16px; }
- .panel-head { margin-bottom: 8px; }
- .panel-head h2 { font-size: 18px; }
- .panel-kicker { margin-bottom: 4px; }
- .pause-stats { margin-bottom: 8px; gap: 5px; }
- .pause-stats div { padding: 4px 8px; }
- .pause-stats b { font-size: 14px; }
- .menu-actions { gap: 5px; }
- .btn { padding: 6px 10px; }
- .btn-primary .btn-title { font-size: 13px; }
- .modal-note { display: none; }
- .btn small already hidden by existing media query.
This should cut roughly: modal padding 52->24 (-28), head 18 -> 8 plus heading smaller (-15), stats height maybe 2 rows ~100 -> 70 (-30), actions 3 buttons 3*~34 + gaps vs current 3*~40 -> maybe -18. Total -90, bringing ~420 to 330. Good.

Also help modal in landscape may be very tall; it will scroll. The help screen has 2 cards + wide card; maybe needs scroll. Fine, but could also compact. Inventory fits.

Also settings modal in portrait fits; in landscape height maybe 500 and overflows. Let's check after CSS.

Add media query for max-height 520 landscape, more general than 430. But phones landscape can be 390 height; small tablets 600. For max-height 520:
- .dim-screen .modal { padding: 14px 18px; }
- hide modal-note
- compact pause-stats and buttons.
However for the menu (menu-screen) there's already max-height 430 rules. We can add a new @media (max-height: 520px) and (orientation: landscape) block after existing. Avoid affecting menu? .modal-scoped only. Fine.

